WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.853
India buys grain at support prices,

2
00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.811
and stores it for food security.

3
00:00:05.369 --> 00:00:07.325
Under WTO farm rules, that

4
00:00:07.325 --> 00:00:08.680
support has a cap:

5
00:00:08.796 --> 00:00:11.257
10 percent of the crop's value,

6
00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:14.674
priced at 1986-88 prices.

7
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.021
Cross it, and India could

8
00:00:17.021 --> 00:00:18.541
face a WTO dispute.

9
00:00:18.874 --> 00:00:20.346
Unless the peace clause applies.

10
00:00:20.605 --> 00:00:22.376
Agreed at Bali in 2013,

11
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:24.542
and extended in 2014 until

12
00:00:24.542 --> 00:00:26.736
a permanent solution is found,

13
00:00:27.011 --> 00:00:29.084
it stops members from challenging

14
00:00:29.084 --> 00:00:30.591
staple-crop stockholding

15
00:00:30.591 --> 00:00:31.408
in a dispute.

16
00:00:31.735 --> 00:00:33.558
India first invoked it in

17
00:00:33.558 --> 00:00:34.652
2020, for rice,

18
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.743
and has invoked it again since.

19
00:00:37.065 --> 00:00:39.330
But there is still no permanent solution,

20
00:00:39.776 --> 00:00:42.408
not even at the WTO's March

21
00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.845
2026 ministerial meeting.

22
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:45.746
A shield,

23
00:00:46.049 --> 00:00:47.054
not a settlement.

24
00:00:47.471 --> 00:00:47.996
Your turn.

25
00:00:48.389 --> 00:00:50.164
What does the peace clause protect?
